OL,3,GNEWSAAsbestos mystery leaves beloved
OL,4,Abeach closed
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor more than six years, asbestos has
OL,7,Fbeen washing up with the tide, turning
OL,8,Fone of Plymouth's handful of swimming
OL,9,Fspots into the centre of a growing
OL,10,Fenvironmental mystery.
OL,12,FMount Batten Beach has been fenced off
OL,13,Fsince the summer, and access restricted
OL,14,Fto two other areas on the peninsula.
OL,16,FIt comes after tests in April and July
OL,17,Ffound asbestos fibres in sand samples
OL,18,Fat levels that could pose a risk to
OL,19,Fhealth if inhaled, Plymouth City
OL,20,FCouncil said.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
